      "title": "Markets freed friendship",
      "gist": "Because relational societies restrict and exclude, modern markets that let people support themselves independently have allowed friendship to become freer and less transactional, a shift the Scottish Enlightenment thinkers like Adam Smith first recognized, though this independence may be fragile."
    },
